INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - DAY

ZAYAN (9) stands in front of the glass trophy case. He is a South Asian boy with tight dark curls and scuffed white trainers.

He wears a bright red hoodie with a frayed left cuff.

Inside the case sits the GIGA-GLOW MEGA-BOT. It is a shiny blue action figure with golden wings. It is the ultimate prize for the weekly challenge.

Zayan bounces on his toes. His eyes dart from the toy, to a flyer on the wall, to a flickering fluorescent light above.

His left hand twitches. Around his wrist is a thick blue RUBBER BAND.

He wants that Mega-Bot. He wants it more than anything.

INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

MR. JASON stands at the whiteboard. He writes with slow, agonizing strokes.

MR. JASON
To win the Mega-Bot, you must solve this sequence. Write your answers clearly.

Zayan sits at his desk. His legs bounce like pistons. 

His brain is already ten steps ahead. He sees the answer instantly. It is a pattern. Red, blue, blue, green.

He grabs his pencil. He tries to write. 

His hand cannot keep up with his thoughts. He scribbles furiously. The lead digs deep. 

Rip! The paper tears.

Zayan gasps. He tries to erase it, but the eraser smudges the graphite into a dark cloud.

Zayan has Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder, which means his brain sees every single possibility at once. Right now, it feels like a TV station playing ten channels on one screen.

Other kids are already writing neatly. 

MAYA (9), sitting next to him, looks over. She has neat braids and a perfectly organized pencil case.

MAYA
Are you okay, Zayan? You are tearing your page.

ZAYAN
My hand is too slow. My head is already on the next page. It is annoying.

He feels the familiar sting in his chest. He assumes he is about to get in trouble for being messy. 

He snaps the blue rubber band on his wrist. 

Snap!

The sharp pinch grounds him. He takes a breath.

Suddenly, the floor vibrates.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

A deep rumble echoes through the school. The lockers shake.

Mr. Jason runs to the door. 

MR. JASON
Everyone stay in your seats!

But the corridor outside is changing. 

With a metallic screech, a massive concrete wall slides out from the side. It blocks the classroom door. 

Another wall slides down from the ceiling. The school is shifting.

Zayan runs to the window. Outside, the playground is gone. Only high, moving stone walls remain.

The school has transformed into a giant maze.

INT. CLASSROOM - LATER

The rumbling stops. The classroom door is completely blocked. 

But a new opening has appeared in the back wall, leading into a dark, unfamiliar corridor.

MR. JASON
I will go look for help. Stay here.

Mr. Jason steps through the back opening. 

Thirty seconds pass.

Slam! 

A wall slides down, cutting Mr. Jason off from the class.

Maya gasps.

MAYA
He is trapped!

LEO (9), a quiet boy with thick glasses, looks at his watch.

LEO
We are all trapped. How do we get out?

Zayan walks to the opening. His eyes trace the seams in the floor. He sees scratches. He sees patterns.

ZAYAN
They are moving. The walls. They do not just slide. They rotate.

MAYA
That is impossible. Schools do not rotate.

ZAYAN
This one does. Look at the dust lines on the floor.

He points to parallel tracks in the linoleum. 

Zayan's mind starts racing. The flickering light, the hum of the walls, the dust—it all fits together. He sees the maze in his head like a giant, ticking clock.

LEO
We should wait.

ZAYAN
We cannot wait. The air vents are closing. If we do not get to the main lobby in five minutes, the automated locks will shut us in for the weekend.

He wants to get to that lobby. He wants to prove he can do this. And he still wants that Mega-Bot.

ZAYAN (CONT'D)
Follow me. I know the way.

INT. SHIFTING CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

Zayan steps into the corridor. Maya and Leo follow closely.

The walls are metallic grey. They hum with power.

ZAYAN
Okay, so the left wall moves every thirty seconds. The right wall moves every forty-five. That means every ninety seconds, they both move at the same time.

He speaks so fast the words blend together.

MAYA
Slow down, Zayan! You are talking in circles.

LEO
I do not see any pattern. It just looks like walls.

Zayan clenches his fists. He hates being slowed down. He hates that his brain is flying while they are walking.

ZAYAN
(to himself)
Why can they not see it? It is right there.

He feels the familiar fear. The fear that his brain is just broken. That he is just a disruptive kid who cannot explain himself.

Suddenly, a wall ahead starts to slide shut.

MAYA
Run!

ZAYAN
No! Stop! 

He grabs Maya's backpack and pulls her back.

Slam!

The wall crashes down right in front of them. A blast of wind ruffles their hair.

ZAYAN (CONT'D)
If we ran, we would have been stuck. We have to wait for the next shift. Exactly twelve seconds.

Maya stares at the wall, then at Zayan. Her eyes are wide.

MAYA
How did you know that?

ZAYAN
Because the blue lights on the panels flash three times before the gears turn. See?

He points to a tiny blue LED on the wall. It flashes once. Twice. Three times.

Click. The wall slides open again.

Leo gasps.

LEO
You are actually tracking all of this.

ZAYAN
I have to. My brain does not have an off switch. It tracks everything.

INT. THE MAZE - CONTINUOUS

They walk deeper into the maze. The grinding of gears grows louder.

It is deafening. The sound bounces off the metal walls.

Zayan covers his ears. The noise is too much. His thoughts start to scramble. 

He cannot see the patterns anymore. The hum of the lights, the grinding of the gears, the panic in Leo's eyes—it is all crashing together.

ZAYAN
(muttering)
Too loud. It is too loud.

MAYA
Zayan? Which way? The wall behind us is moving!

Zayan freezes. He looks left. He looks right. Both paths look identical. His brain is spinning.

He feels like he is failing. 

He reaches down. He grabs the blue rubber band on his wrist.

Snap!

The sharp pinch clears the noise.

He focuses on the physical sensation. The pain fades, leaving a clear line of sight.

He looks at the dust on the floor. Left path has more dust. That means it has not moved in a while. It is due to shift.

ZAYAN
Right! Go right! Now!

They sprint to the right.

Slam!

The left path closes behind them, sealing off the dust.

INT. THE ROTUNDA - CONTINUOUS

They emerge into a large, circular room. 

In the center of the room is the glass display case. The Giga-Glow Mega-Bot shines under a spotlight.

Beyond the case is the exit doors. They are slowly sliding shut.

LEO
There is the exit! But look at the floor!

The floor of the rotunda is made of concentric rings. They are spinning in opposite directions.

MAYA
We will never cross that. It is moving too fast.

Zayan steps to the edge. He watches the spinning rings.

To Maya and Leo, it is a blur of motion.

To Zayan, it is a grid. He sees the gaps aligning. He sees the rhythm.

ZAYAN
It is a triple spiral. Every five seconds, the gaps line up for one-tenth of a second.

MAYA
We cannot jump that fast!

ZAYAN
We do not have to jump. We just have to run at a diagonal. Follow my steps. Exactly where I step.

Leo looks terrified.

LEO
Are you sure, Zayan?

Zayan looks at his friends. He does not see doubt in their eyes anymore. He sees trust.

ZAYAN
I am sure. Trust my fast brain.

He takes a deep breath. He does not snap the rubber band this time. He does not need to. His mind is perfectly aligned with the spinning room.

ZAYAN (CONT'D)
Three... two... one... GO!

Zayan leaps onto the first ring. He runs at an angle.

Maya steps exactly where he stepped.

Leo follows.

The floor spins beneath them, but they are moving with the flow, crossing from ring to ring just as the gaps align.

It is like walking on water.

They reach the center platform. 

Zayan grabs the latch of the display case. He swings it open and snatches the Giga-Glow Mega-Bot.

MAYA
The door is closing!

The exit doors are almost shut. Only a small gap remains.

ZAYAN
Slide!

Zayan slides on his stomach across the polished floor. 

Maya and Leo slide right behind him.

They shoot through the gap just as the heavy steel doors slam shut.

INT. SCHOOL LOBBY - CONTINUOUS

They crash into a heap on the lobby floor.

They are safe. 

Outside, the sun is shining. The normal school bells ring. 

Behind them, the heavy doors remain shut, but the rumbling has stopped.

Zayan sits up. He is breathing hard. He still has the Mega-Bot in his hand.

Maya laughs, throwing her hands in the air.

MAYA
We made it! We actually made it!

LEO
That was amazing. Zayan, you are a genius.

ZAYAN
I am not a genius. My brain just works in fast-forward.

MAYA
Well, I am glad it does. I would still be stuck in the classroom trying to pack my pencils.

She smiles. It is a warm, genuine smile.

Zayan looks down at the Mega-Bot. He holds it out to Maya and Leo.

ZAYAN
We solved the sequence together. We share it.

Leo takes the toy, grinning.

LEO
I get it on weekends.

MAYA
Deal.

Zayan stands up. His legs are still bouncing. He cannot help it. He snaps his rubber band gently, just to feel the rhythm.

He still has ADHD. He still has a messy desk and torn papers waiting for him. But today, he knows his fast brain is exactly what they needed.

He smiles, ready for whatever shift comes next.